    "result": "I've already completed this implementation! Here's what was done:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n**CLI (`packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`):**\n- Added `threshold?: string[]` to `EvalOptions` \n- Added `--threshold <metric=min>` option with accumulator for multiple values\n- Created `parseThresholds()` to validate format and 0-1 range\n- Updated `runEvalCommand()` to:\n  - Validate all threshold metrics exist in evaluations\n  - Pass thresholds to `generateReport()`\n  - Exit 2 on malformed or unknown metrics (before writing report)\n  - Exit 1 if `report.passed === false`, 0 otherwise\n\n**SDK (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js`):**\n- Updated `generateReport()` to accept optional `thresholds` parameter\n- Adds `passed` boolean and `thresholds` array to report when thresholds provided\n- Each threshold: `{ metric, min, score, passed }`\n- Metrics with `score === null` fail their threshold\n\n**Reporting (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js`):**\n- Markdown: Added \"Thresholds\" section with PASS/FAIL status per threshold\n- JSON: Fields auto-included (no changes needed)\n\n**Tests (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js`):**\n- Thresholds that pass\n- Thresholds that fail  \n- Metrics with no score failing thresholds\n\n**Documentation:**\n- Updated README.md files for both CLI and SDK\n\n## Key Behaviors\n\n\u2705 No `--threshold` \u2192 original behavior unchanged  \n\u2705 Multiple thresholds: `--threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.95`  \n\u2705 Exit codes: 0 (all pass), 1 (any fail), 2 (usage error)  \n\u2705 Report written both ways; just not written on exit 2  \n\u2705 Works with custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations()`\n\nIs there something specific about the implementation you'd like me to adjust or verify?",
